.TH SDL_GetRenderLogicalPresentation 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetRenderLogicalPresentation \- Get device independent resolution and presentation mode for rendering.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetRenderLogicalPresentation(SDL_Renderer *renderer, int *w, int *h, SDL_RendererLogicalPresentation *mode);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function gets the width and height of the logical rendering output, or 0 if a logical resolution is not enabled\[char46]
.PP
Each render target has its own logical presentation state\[char46] This function gets the state for the current render target\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.TP
.I w
an int filled with the logical presentation width\[char46]
.TP
.I h
an int filled with the logical presentation height\[char46]
.TP
.I mode
a variable filled with the logical presentation mode being used\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetRenderLogicalPresentation (3)
